# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repository is worked on from Windows/WSL and from Linux, and the round
# trip had silently rewritten committed LF files to CRLF in the working tree.
# For shell scripts that is not cosmetic: a `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` shebang, or
# `set -euo pipefail\r`, does not run. scripts/dod.sh — the Definition of Done
# gate — could not execute at all in that state, on any platform.
#
# Deliberately narrow rather than a blanket `* text=auto`: a repo-wide
# normalisation would rewrite hundreds of files at once and bury real changes.

# Anything executed by a shell or copied into a Linux container must be LF.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# PowerShell is run from Windows; CRLF is correct there.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Python tolerates either, but the tree is LF and mixed endings make diffs
# unreadable — a two-line change shows as a whole-file rewrite.
*.py        text eol=lf

*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.docx      binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.iso       binary
